{"parentUuid":"61183f86-8677-4d39-8059-67148755e933","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/alex/workspace/cli","sessionId":"0cf3db51-1c73-43bb-8d05-dc02739514a5","version":"2.1.14","gitBranch":"alex/ent-109-text-output-checkpoint-flag","slug":"delegated-sauteeing-moon","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01EBzjemSDLVnxNyeKeUfjgt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see we use PostToolUse for:\n- `Task` tool (subagent completion)\n- `TodoWrite` tool (todo updates)\n\nWe could add PostToolUse for file-modifying tools like `Edit`, `Write`, `Bash`. But that would be very chatty - every file edit would trigger a checkpoint.\n\nA more targeted approach: checkpoint when specific \"milestones\" happen:\n1. PostToolUse[Bash] when the bash command contains \"git add\" or \"git commit\" - indicates user is committing\n2. But wait, the user makes commits directly, not through Claude\n\nActually, the git hooks (prepare-commit-msg, post-commit) ARE the right place. The question is what they should do.\n\nLet me think about this differently:\n\nCurrent problem: \n- Shadow branch content gets condensed and deleted on commit\n- Next commit has no shadow branch content to condense\n- System thinks \"no new content\" and tries to reuse checkpoint\n- But BaseCommit drifted, so it picks wrong session\n\nAlternative approach:\n- Don't delete shadow branch until session ends?\n- Or: re-create shadow branch from transcript on next checkpoint event?\n\nActually, the simplest fix might be:\n- On post-commit, ALWAYS update BaseCommit to new HEAD\n- This keeps the session \"current\" even when there's no new content\n- Then subsequent commits can correctly find the current session\n\nLet me propose this to the user. It's a minimal fix that addresses the immediate bug. The larger question of \"should we checkpoint on every commit\" is a design change that could be addressed separately.","signature":""}],"stop_reas