re not in `FilesTouched`\n- So the file overlap check would fail, and we wouldn't add a trailer\n\nBut wait, the current logic is:\n```goif session.LastCheckpointID != \"\" &&\n   (len(session.FilesTouched) == 0 || hasOverlappingFiles(stagedFiles, session.FilesTouched)) {\n    checkpointID = session.LastCheckpointID\n\n\n```\n\nThis handles reuse—it reuses the old checkpoint ID only if no files were tracked or if there's overlap. For the new checkpoint case when the transcript grows, I should apply the same file overlap check. If the human commits files that Claude never touched, there's no reason to link them to Claude's session with a trailer at all.\n\nSo the approach is: first check whether committed files overlap with FilesTouched. If there's no overlap, skip the trailer entirely. If there is overlap, then decide between reusing the existing checkpoint ID (when lastCheckpointId exists and the transcript hasn't grown) or generating a new one.\n\n```","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":401,"cache_read_input_tokens":89502,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":401,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CXLNmc8TuG5YL35x4UM8V","type":"assistant","uuid":"cef8df5e-773d-4413-9e20-070e0210d991","timestamp":"2026-01-21T10:36:49.337Z"}
