{"parentUuid":"04844163-f5e1-4ad5-a0f5-939dd9bcca93","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/alex/workspace/cli","sessionId":"0cf3db51-1c73-43bb-8d05-dc02739514a5","version":"2.1.14","gitBranch":"alex/ent-112-checkpoint-id-reuse-bug","slug":"delegated-sauteeing-moon","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XSQBYSTBaUh5JdJpm6qWx3","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":\"6989c591-1d83-43bf-b53d-0b956f8e7697\",\"identifier\":\"ENT-112\",\"title\":\"Checkpoint ID reuse bugs: stale BaseCommit fallback + transcript growth not checked\",\"description\":\"## Overview\\n\\nTwo related bugs in checkpoint ID reuse logic that can cause commits to link to incorrect or stale checkpoint metadata.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Problem 1: Cleared lastCheckpointId causing fallback to old sessions (FIXED)\\n\\n### Scenario\\n\\n1. **Commit 1**: Claude works → Stop → commit → condensation\\n   * `lastCheckpointId` = \\\"abc123\\\"\\n2. **New prompt arrives** (UserPromptSubmit - queued message)\\n   * `lastCheckpointId` **cleared to \\\"\\\"**\\n3. Claude works (no Stop yet)\\n4. **Commit 2**: Claude commits\\n   * Current session: `lastCheckpointId` = \\\"\\\" → **skipped**\\n   * No sessions have `lastCheckpointId` to reuse among sessions matching HEAD\\n   * Fallback to ALL sessions triggered\\n   * Old session from days ago has `lastCheckpointId` + overlapping files\\n   * **Result**: Old session's checkpoint ID incorrectly used\\n\\n### Root Cause\\n\\n1. `lastCheckpointId` cleared on new prompt, making current session ineligible for reuse\\n2. Fallback logic included ALL sessions in worktree when none had valid `lastCheckpointId`\\n3. Old session matched because it still had `lastCheckpointId` set and overlapping `FilesTouched`\\n\\n### Proposed Fix\\n\\n1. Remove fallback - if no sessions match HEAD with valid `lastCheckpointId`, don't add trailer (`manual_commit_hooks.go:220-230`)\\n2. Also: Update `BaseCommit` for all sessions even when no content to condense (`manual_commit_hooks.go:389-404`)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Problem 2: Reusing checkpoint ID when transcript has grown\\n\\n### Scenario\\n\\n1. **Commit 1**: Claude works → Stop event → commit\\n   * Condensation happens\\n   * `lastCheckpointId` = \\\"abc123\\\"\\n   * Metadata on `entire/sessions` has transcript lines 1-989\\n   * `condensedTranscriptLines` = 989\\n2. **Commit 2**: Claude continues working → transcript grows to 1305 lines → Claude commits (no Stop event yet)\\n   * No shadow branch exists (deleted after Commit 1)\\n   * `lastCheckpointId` = \\\"abc123\\\" still set (no prompt to clear it)\\n   * Reuse logic kicks in → checkpoint \\\"abc123\\\" is used\\n   * **Result**: Commit 2 links to checkpoint \\\"abc123\\\" which only has lines 1-989\\n   * **Lines 990-1305 are not captured in any checkpoint**\\n\\n### Root Cause\\n\\nThe reuse logic checks:\\n\\n* `lastCheckpointId != \\\"\\\"`\\n* `FilesTouched` empty OR overlapping with staged files\\n\\nBut does NOT check whether the transcript has grown since the last condensation.\\n\\n### Proposed Fix\\n\\nBefore reusing `lastCheckpointId`, check actual transcript line count vs `condensedTranscriptLines`:\\n\\n```go\\nif currentTranscriptLines > session.CondensedTranscriptLines {\\n    // Transcript has grown - Claude has been working\\n    // Can't reuse old checkpoint ID - would link to stale metadata\\n    continue\\n}\\n```\\n\\nThis ensures reuse only happens when Claude is truly dormant (transcript unchanged), not when Claude is actively working.\",\"projectMilestone\":{\"id\":\"f0e6842e-d86f-4a14-9808-610ec86a3ad1\",\"name\":\"R1\"},\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/ENT-112/checkpoint-id-reuse-bugs-stale-basecommit-fallback-transcript-growth\",\"gitBranchName\":\"alex/ent-112-checkpoint-id-reuse-bugs-stale-basecommit-fallback\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-01-21T09:37:54.792Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-01-21T09:43:56.284Z\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"labels\":[\